Corp.&#148; to &#147;Aeries Technology, Inc.&#148;, (ii) making ATI&#146;s corporate existence perpetual, and (iii)&nbsp;removing certain provisions related to our status as a blank check company
that will no longer be applicable upon consummation of the Business Combination, all of which the board of directors of WWAC believes are necessary to adequately address the needs of the Combined Company after the Business Combination. We refer to
this proposal as &#147;<U>Governing Documents Proposal C</U>.&#148; </P></TD></TR></TABLE> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
